3.1:
On my bed at night 
I sought the beloved of my being; 
I sought him, but I did not find him.

5.1:
I have come to my garden, 
My sister, my bride; 
I have plucked my myrrh with my spice; 
I have eaten my honeycomb with my honey; 
I have drunk my wine with my milk. 
Eat, O friends! 
Drink, and drink deeply, 
O beloved ones!

5.11:
His head is refined gold; 
His locks are wavy, 
Black as a raven.

7.5:
Your head upon you is like Mount Karmel, 
And the hair of your head like purple; 
The meleḵ is held captive, by the ringlets.

7.11:
Come, my beloved, 
Let us go forth to the field; 
Let us stay in the villages.

8.6:
Put me as a seal upon your heart, 
As a seal upon your arm; 
For love is as strong as death, 
Jealousy as cruel as the grave; 
Its flames are flames of fire, 
A flame of Yah!

8.11:
Shelomoh had a vineyard 
In Ba’al Hamon; 
He let out the vineyard to keepers; 
Each one was to bring for its fruit 
A thousand pieces of silver.

8.13:
You who sit in the gardens, 
The companions listen for your voice; 
Let me hear it!
